Since talk about a theoretical reimplementation of RSTS/E isn't really 
meaningful at this point, I'll just stick with the current RSTS/E on PDP-11.
Of course it can be done. It should in fact be almost trivially straight 
forward. You write the RTS. The RTS have vectors for some various 
instructions, such as EMT. Unix programs do EMTs for system calls. You 
translate the Unix system calls that are possible into RSTS/E calls 
