Except for the DS15, I wouldn't call the models you listed "desktop 
machines". 

Let aside the size (and noise), the models you are looking for were 
mostly sold as "AlphaServer". The difference between them and the 
respective "AlphaStation" models was mainly a (reasonable) graphics 
adapter; so if you get hold of an AlphaServer DSxx/ESxx, just look for a 
graphics card supported by OpenVMS and you have your "AlphaStation".

Probably an XP1000 or XP900 (actually a DS10) are easier to find (and 
pay) than the larger boxes in your list.

Hans.


