The 11/782 and 11/785 are not really comparable, in that the 11/782 was
an ASMP machine, and the 11/785 was a conventional uniprocessor system.

That said, I've never seen the 11/780-2 designation before.

The purchase order for the first 11/780 (sold to Carnegie-Mellon 
University) referred to the system as a PDP-11/780.

This PO was on display at the 10th Anniversary celebration for the VAX 
at the fall 1987 DECUS symposium in Anaheim, CA.

                      -- Rob


